hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18196","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam who said: Abu Hasan narrated to me that Amr ibn Murrah said to Muawiyah: O Muawiyah, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no imam or governor who closes his door against those in need, want and poverty, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, closes the doors of heaven against his need, want and poverty. He said: So Muawiyah appointed a man over the needs of the people."
